Before you burn & rebuild a system, you should be sure to inventory all of your 
licenses ("lmf list") to make sure you know what the system thinks you've got. 
If you can't find paper certificates for all of them, you can use the lmf 
"issue" command to remove them into text files before you shut down.  Copy the 
saved files to a floppy for safe-keeping, and you can re-register them from the 
files again once you've reinstalled unix.   (man lmf for details)



