To configure audit you should use the Audit Configuration menu
(see the SysMan Configuration menu).  If you have not already
Configured Audit on your system, this will rebuild your kernel
with Audit Configured and you will have to reboot.  If you have
already configured audit, but not enabled it, this will enable it
with the parameters you set.

For more information on Audit, see the Security manual and
the auditd and auditmask man pages.

